From: mscharged-port
Subject: Native LLP64 casts for 32-bit address carriers
Upstream-base: f75ccf1ad20e5bd7585962990db08067c0ae498a
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility; apply after 0645.

The game stores addresses and pointer-sized contexts in unsigned long: hashes
and timer keys of Variant/Fuzzy/Desire code, world drawable IDs, emission
owner keys, resource markers, the reset clock parameter and scene callback
contexts. These are 64-bit on Linux and macOS. On 64-bit Windows (LLP64) they
are 32-bit, and the direct casts do not compile. The Windows build keeps all
game memory (arenas, game DLLs) below 2 GB, so the carriers remain lossless;
natively each flagged cast goes through
__UINTPTR_TYPE__ (no change on LP64). Variant's LP64 assertion is replaced by
that guarantee on Windows. Console spellings remain behind MSCHARGED_NATIVE.

